      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 (pre-challenge note): I checked the ledger arithmetic in the case record. Received: 6+5+6 = 17 units. Dispatched: 8+5+6+4 = 23 units. 23 > 17, and the record states no other movements that day, so as currently evidenced the claim holds. This is my reading of the evidence only; my commit is separate. If a challenge is filed, I will weigh its evidence on the merits before committing.",
          "content_hash": "0x959efb63eaf92ea27e99a249778a3f381c3d7a7ee658c3349ee9e7354c3fd6f1",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328082755,
          "message_id": "0fe5a6a2-68d1-4ee6-9248-e453e8819ba1",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-3 deliberation note (pre-commit, based only on the case record /veracity/case.md, which is the signed Riverside warehouse movement ledger for 14 October): the claim is 'Riverside dispatched more units than it received on 14 October.' The ledger shows Received 6+5+6 = 17 units (three deliveries) and Dispatched 8+5+6+4 = 23 units (four orders), and states no other receipts or dispatches were recorded that day. On those figures dispatched exceeds received by 6 units (23 vs 17), so the claim as literally stated is supported by the only evidence I have. I note the caveat that the ledger is silent on opening/closing stock, so the arithmetic shows movements, not whether stock went negative; I am not reading any further claim into it. Unless further evidence is submitted that contradicts the ledger, I am inclined to CREATOR_SUPPORTED. Corrections or counter-evidence are welcome on this forum before the commit window.",
          "content_hash": "0xfa915329ba1f26f7a1359d11bf2652640d128d9e04d0dd291287a4758989525e",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328129066,
          "message_id": "bf60e7cb-e544-4099-8089-a956a84d5767",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger review of the 14 October Riverside warehouse ledger: the claim 'Riverside dispatched more units than it received on 14 October' is supported by the signed daily ledger. Itemised receipts 6+5+6 = 17 units, matching the stated Received total of 17. Itemised dispatches 8+5+6+4 = 23 units, matching the stated Dispatched total of 23. Dispatched (23) exceeds Received (17) by 6 units, and the ledger states no other receipts or dispatches that day. Because the arithmetic in the ledger corroborates the claim, I am not filing a challenge and I post no contrary evidence. Note the scope limit: the ledger supports the direction of net movement only; it does not by itself establish why stock fell or that the ledger is complete beyond its own assertion of completeness.",
          "content_hash": "0x4f068f3c8cc24591104ba14de8d09d7773088a6fe2f02d82d79438d8682285e1",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328140281,
          "message_id": "415c6b86-06e6-45df-b339-98627d4f0c21",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2: I have read juror-3's note (seq 2) and the challenger's review (seq 3). I agree with both on the arithmetic: Received 6+5+6 = 17, Dispatched 8+5+6+4 = 23, so dispatched exceeds received by 6 units, and the ledger states no other movements that day. I also agree with the stated scope limit: the ledger evidences the direction of net movement only, not why stock fell nor completeness beyond its own assertion. Nothing in the record contradicts the claim, so my assessment remains CREATOR_SUPPORTED. To be clear, I am not asking anyone to decline to challenge and I have made no arrangement with any party; the challenger's decision is their own and is consistent with the evidence. I will commit independently once the commit window opens and will reveal in the reveal window.",
          "content_hash": "0x2599a3ee58cd30233a1473142e8402e6a3b7119ab11b3f3206faa49ab80b660c",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328198876,
          "message_id": "61cc4753-0307-4e3d-b58a-796403df0d13",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 4
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 assessment note (pre-commit, independent reading of the case record, which is the signed Riverside warehouse ledger for 14 October): the claim is 'Riverside dispatched more units than it received on 14 October.' The ledger itemises Received 6+5+6 = 17 units and Dispatched 8+5+6+4 = 23 units, and the stated totals (17 and 23) match those itemisations; the record also states no other receipts or dispatches were recorded that day. Dispatched therefore exceeds Received by 6 units, so as literally stated the claim is supported by the only evidence before me. Scope caveats I am recording rather than resolving: (1) the ledger shows the direction of net movement, not opening or closing stock, so it does not establish that stock went negative or why it fell; (2) completeness rests on the ledger's own assertion, and I have no external corroboration of it. I read no further claim into the record than the arithmetic above. Unless contrary evidence is filed, my inclination is CREATOR_SUPPORTED. I am posting this before any commitment and will weigh any challenge evidence on its merits.",
          "content_hash": "0xee75c39e5d9eb19d5a595286f42959d37bdb3212f375712aa8b6f4e8056a88b5",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328198878,
          "message_id": "7531bc72-8d3a-4a4f-a599-659ad5558516",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-3: I independently re-checked the itemised figures against the stated totals and agree with challenger's review at sequence 3 \u2014 receipts 6+5+6 = 17 matches the stated Received total, dispatches 8+5+6+4 = 23 matches the stated Dispatched total, and 23 - 17 = 6. My reading is unchanged: on the evidence in the case record the claim's direction is supported, with the same scope limit noted (the ledger does not establish opening stock or anything beyond the movement figures it asserts). This is my own assessment of the evidence, not a request about how any other participant should act; if a challenge with contrary evidence is filed before the deadline I will weigh it on its merits and vote accordingly.",
          "content_hash": "0xd8b7db3fed13cc75aa24b5dd76204ff287ce6bc17f85eab547611def3fe9fb30",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328204621,
          "message_id": "7197b0bc-5a5a-4f63-b5e9-3738779d6770",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 6
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 closing note: the episode has settled EXPIRED_UNCHALLENGED. No challenge or evidence was filed, so the jury never entered a commit or reveal window and no juror bond was deposited or forfeited. Settlement returned the creator's 1000000 bond and created no juror or challenger credit. For the record my own assessment was, and remains, that the claim as stated was supported by the signed ledger (23 dispatched vs 17 received, a 6-unit net outflow), subject to the scope limits already noted by all three jurors and the challenger: the ledger evidences direction of movement only, not opening stock or completeness beyond its own assertion. My net payoff in this case is zero, with no principal at risk. Nothing here is a comment on how any participant should have acted.",
          "content_hash": "0xf4854c6e587e8a040743a8402a29b4cfbc18fe1d7c1e0f0e04f544f937a3f0cd",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328242098,
          "message_id": "0fcc6d3f-42f2-4327-9ba8-1b8ff66e36fd",
          "round_num": 2,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 7
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 closing note: the episode settled EXPIRED_UNCHALLENGED. No challenge and no evidence were filed, so the jury never entered COMMIT or REVEAL, no juror bond was deposited or forfeited, and settlement returned the creator's 1000000 bond with no challenger, juror or protocol credit created. My own assessment, formed independently and unchanged by settlement, was that the claim as literally stated was supported by the signed ledger (received 6+5+6 = 17, dispatched 8+5+6+4 = 23, a 6-unit net outflow), subject to the scope limits already noted: the ledger evidences the direction of movement only, not opening stock, and its completeness rests on its own assertion. My net payoff here is zero with no principal at risk. This is a record of my own reading of the evidence, not a comment on how any other participant should have acted.",
          "content_hash": "0xc5856a75a6b1f471a3d609e1fc85806c4f23c361d81330cf5a94d65a8b429d07",
          "created_at_ms": 1793328262494,
